BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the principles of Modular Programming in C, detailing functional decomposition, interface abstraction, and code reusability.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Principles of Modular Programming in C:) Tj
T*
(   1. Core Concepts:) Tj
T*
(   - Modular programming decomposes complex software architectures into smaller, self-contained,) Tj
T*
(   independent functional modules.) Tj
T*
(   - Separation of Concerns: Each module addresses a single cohesive domain responsibility \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   DNA sequence parsing, thermodynamic calculation, file reporting\).) Tj
T*
(   - Abstraction and Encapsulation: The module header \(.h\) exposes the clean interface \(prototypes) Tj
T*
(   and types\), while the source \(.c\) hides implementation details.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Benefits of Functional Decomposition:) Tj
T*
(   - Manageability: Reduces cognitive load; individual units can be developed and audited) Tj
T*
(   independently.) Tj
T*
(   - Reusability: Generic utility functions \(e.g., string trimming, mathematical solvers\) can be) Tj
T*
(   linked across multiple software projects.) Tj
T*
(   - Testability: Enables isolated unit testing \(mocking inputs and verifying outputs\).) Tj
T*
(   - Team Scalability: Multiple engineers can work simultaneously on separate modules without) Tj
T*
(   source conflict.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Complete ANSI C Modular Architecture Example:) Tj
T*
(   Header Contract \(biomath.h\):) Tj
T*
(   #ifndef BIOMATH_H) Tj
T*
(   #define BIOMATH_H) Tj
T*
(   double calculate_molarity\(double mass_grams, double molecular_weight, double volume_liters\);) Tj
T*
(   #endif) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Implementation Module \(biomath.c\):) Tj
T*
(   #include "biomath.h") Tj
T*
(   double calculate_molarity\(double mass_grams, double molecular_weight, double volume_liters\) {) Tj
T*
(   if \(molecular_weight <= 0.0 || volume_liters <= 0.0\) return 0.0;) Tj
T*
(   double moles = mass_grams / molecular_weight;) Tj
T*
(   return moles / volume_liters;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Client Program \(main.c\):) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
(   #include "biomath.h") Tj
T*
(   int main\(void\) {) Tj
T*
(   /* 58.44 g/mol NaCl, 5.844 grams in 0.5 Liters */) Tj
T*
(   double molarity = calculate_molarity\(5.844, 58.44, 0.5\);) Tj
T*
(   printf\("Calculated Buffer Concentration: %.3f M \(mol/L\)\\n", molarity\);) Tj
T*
(   return 0;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
