(   [Problem Statement]: Compare Call-by-Value with Call-by-Reference in C, illustrating stack frame isolation and pointer-based parameter modification.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Call-by-Value vs Simulated Call-by-Reference in C:) Tj
T*
(   1. Fundamental Mechanism in C:) Tj
T*
(   Strict Rule: The C programming language supports ONLY Call-by-Value natively!) Tj
T*
(   - Every argument passed into a function is evaluated and copied into a fresh local variable on) Tj
T*
(   the callee's stack frame.) Tj
T*
(   - Changes made to formal parameters inside the function affect ONLY the local copies; the) Tj
T*
(   caller's variables remain untouched.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Simulating Call-by-Reference via Pointers:) Tj
T*
(   To modify caller variables, programmers pass memory addresses \(&variable\) as values. The) Tj
T*
(   function receives a pointer and dereferences it \(*ptr\) to modify the caller's memory directly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Stack Frame Memory Walkthrough:) Tj
T*
(   - Call-by-Value:) Tj
T*
(   main frame: [x = 5]) Tj
T*
(   func frame: [a = 5] -> modified to 99 -> destroyed on return!) Tj
T*
(   main frame x remains 5.) Tj
T*
(   - Pointer Pass:) Tj
T*
(   main frame: [x = 5] at address 0x1000) Tj
T*
(   func frame: [ptr = 0x1000] -> writes 99 to address 0x1000!) Tj
T*
(   main frame x is now 99!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Demonstrative ANSI C Program:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   /* Call-by-Value: Ineffective swap */) Tj
T*
(   void swap_by_value\(int a, int b\) {) Tj
T*
(   int temp = a;) Tj
T*
(   a = b;) Tj
T*
(   b = temp;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   /* Simulated Call-by-Reference: Effective swap using pointers */) Tj
T*
(   void swap_by_reference\(int *a, int *b\) {) Tj
T*
(   int temp = *a;) Tj
T*
(   *a = *b;) Tj
T*
(   *b = temp;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int main\(void\) {) Tj
T*
(   int x = 10, y = 20;) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   printf\("Initial: x = %d, y = %d\\n", x, y\);) Tj
T*
(   swap_by_value\(x, y\);) Tj
T*
(   printf\("After swap_by_value: x = %d, y = %d \(Unchanged!\)\\n", x, y\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   swap_by_reference\(&x, &y\);) Tj
T*
(   printf\("After swap_by_reference: x = %d, y = %d \(Successfully Swapped!\)\\n", x, y\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   return 0;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
