BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain array parameter passing in C, detailing array decay to pointers and why array length cannot be determined via sizeof inside functions.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Array Parameter Passing and Decay to Pointers in C:) Tj
T*
(   1. Array Decay Principle:) Tj
T*
(   In C, an array identifier represents a contiguous block of memory. However, when an array is) Tj
T*
(   passed as an argument to a function, it AUTOMATICALLY DECAYS into a pointer to its first) Tj
T*
(   element:) Tj
T*
(   void process_array\(int arr[]\)) Tj
T*
(   is rewritten internally by the compiler as:) Tj
T*
(   void process_array\(int *arr\)) Tj
T*
(   Even if an explicit size is written: void process\(int arr[100]\), the compiler completely) Tj
T*
(   discards '100' and treats it as int *arr.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The sizeof Pitfall Inside Functions:) Tj
T*
(   - In caller scope where array is defined:) Tj
T*
(   int data[50];) Tj
T*
(   sizeof\(data\) == 50 * sizeof\(int\) == 200 bytes.) Tj
T*
(   - Inside callee function:) Tj
T*
(   void func\(int data[]\) {) Tj
T*
(   sizeof\(data\) == sizeof\(int*\) == 8 bytes \(on 64-bit systems\)!) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   Dividing sizeof\(data\) / sizeof\(data[0]\) yields 8 / 4 = 2, REGARDLESS OF ACTUAL ARRAY SIZE!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Architectural Consequence:) Tj
T*
(   Because C pointers carry no metadata regarding array bounds, THE CALLER MUST EXPLICITLY PASS) Tj
T*
(   THE ARRAY LENGTH as an auxiliary parameter!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Complete ANSI C Source Code:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   double compute_mean\(const double *arr, int length\) {) Tj
T*
(   if \(length <= 0\) return 0.0;) Tj
T*
(   double sum = 0.0;) Tj
T*
(   for \(int i = 0; i < length; i++\) {) Tj
T*
(   sum += arr[i];) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   return sum / \(double\)length;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int main\(void\) {) Tj
T*
(   double absorbance_readings[] = {0.125, 0.250, 0.498, 0.742, 1.012};) Tj
T*
(   int n = sizeof\(absorbance_readings\) / sizeof\(absorbance_readings[0]\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   printf\("Caller scope: array memory footprint = %zu bytes\\n", sizeof\(absorbance_readings\)\);) Tj
T*
(   printf\("Number of elements calculated in caller: %d\\n", n\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   double mean_abs = compute_mean\(absorbance_readings, n\);) Tj
T*
(   printf\("Calculated Spectrophotometric Mean Absorbance: %.4f OD\\n", mean_abs\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   return 0;) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
