(>> Solution to Question 5:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain recursion in C, detailing base cases, recursive steps, call stack mechanics, and stack overflow conditions.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Recursion and Call Stack Mechanics in C:) Tj
T*
(   1. Conceptual Definition:) Tj
T*
(   Recursion is a programming technique where a function solves a problem by invoking smaller) Tj
T*
(   instances of itself until a trivial termination condition is satisfied.) Tj
T*
(   Every recursive function must contain two essential components:) Tj
T*
(   - Base Case: A terminating condition that returns a concrete result without making further) Tj
T*
(   recursive calls.) Tj
T*
(   - Recursive Step: A progressive step that breaks the problem into subproblems and invokes the) Tj
T*
(   function recursively, moving strictly closer to the base case.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Call Stack Mechanics and Activation Records:) Tj
T*
(   Each function invocation creates a new Activation Record \(Stack Frame\) on the runtime call) Tj
T*
(   stack:) Tj
T*
(   - Stores parameters, local variables, frame pointer, and return address.) Tj
T*
(   - As recursive calls deepen, stack frames accumulate linearly \(Winding phase\).) Tj
T*
(   - When the base case is reached, frames return values and are popped off the stack \(Unwinding) Tj
T*
(   phase\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Stack Overflow Hazard:) Tj
T*
(   - If the base case is omitted, incorrect, or unreachable, infinite recursion occurs.) Tj
T*
(   - Since stack memory is finite \(typically 1 MB to 8 MB per thread\), runaway recursion exhausts) Tj
T*
(   stack memory, triggering an unrecoverable SIGSEGV segmentation fault.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Factorial Trace Diagram for factorial\(3\):) Tj
T*
(   [call factorial\(3\)] -> pushes Frame 3, waits for factorial\(2\)) Tj
T*
(   [call factorial\(2\)] -> pushes Frame 2, waits for factorial\(1\)) Tj
T*
(   [call factorial\(1\)] -> pushes Frame 1, waits for factorial\(0\)) Tj
T*
(   [call factorial\(0\)] -> Base case reached! Returns 1!) Tj
T*
(   Frame 1 receives 1 -> computes 1 * 1 = 1 -> returns 1) Tj
T*
(   Frame 2 receives 1 -> computes 2 * 1 = 2 -> returns 2) Tj
T*
(   Frame 3 receives 2 -> computes 3 * 2 = 6 -> returns 6!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Complete ANSI C Code:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   unsigned long long recursive_factorial\(unsigned int n\) {) Tj
T*
(   /* 1. Base Case: 0! = 1 */) Tj
T*
(   if \(n == 0\) return 1ULL;) Tj
T*
(   /* 2. Recursive Step */) Tj
T*
(   return \(unsigned long long\)n * recursive_factorial\(n - 1\);) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int main\(void\) {) Tj
T*
(   printf\("5! = %llu\\n", recursive_factorial\(5\)\);) Tj
T*
(   return 0;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
