(   - Declared inside a function block with the 'static' keyword.) Tj
T*
(   - Initialized only ONCE at program startup.) Tj
T*
(   - Unlike auto variables which are wiped upon function exit, local static variables retain their) Tj
T*
(   values across multiple calls:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
(   int generate_sample_id\(void\) {) Tj
T*
(   static int current_id = 1000; /* Stored in data segment, initialized once */) Tj
T*
(   current_id++;) Tj
T*
(   return current_id;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Global Static Variables \(Internal Linkage\):) Tj
T*
(   - Declared outside of all functions with 'static'.) Tj
T*
(   - Restricts symbol visibility STRICTLY TO THE CURRENT TRANSLATION UNIT \(.c file\).) Tj
T*
(   - If file1.c declares static int config_mode = 1; and file2.c also declares static int) Tj
T*
(   config_mode = 2;, NO LINKER COLLISION OCCURS. Each file has its own private, isolated variable.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Global Static Functions \(Private Helper Functions\):) Tj
T*
(   - In C, functions have external linkage by default.) Tj
T*
(   - Marking a function static void parse_internal\(\) limits its accessibility strictly to callers) Tj
T*
(   within the same .c file.) Tj
T*
(   - Crucial Software Engineering Value:) Tj
T*
(   Enforces encapsulation and information hiding. Internal helper functions cannot be called) Tj
T*
(   improperly by external modules, preventing unintended state mutations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
