(   [Problem Statement]: Detail external linkage using extern across multiple source files with an annotated multi-module C project layout.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   External Linkage and the extern Keyword:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition of Linkage:) Tj
T*
(   Linkage describes how names can be shared across multiple compilation units \(source files\).) Tj
T*
(   - External Linkage: Symbol can be referenced across multiple translation units by the linker.) Tj
T*
(   - Internal Linkage: Symbol is restricted to its own translation unit \(static\).) Tj
T*
(   - No Linkage: Symbol is local to a block \(auto/register\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Declaration vs Definition Rule \(One Definition Rule - ODR\):) Tj
T*
(   - Definition: Allocates storage memory for variable: int global_pcr_cycles = 30;) Tj
T*
(   MUST OCCUR IN EXACTLY ONE .c FILE!) Tj
T*
(   - Declaration: Informs compiler of type and name without allocating memory:) Tj
T*
(   extern int global_pcr_cycles;) Tj
T*
(   CAN OCCUR IN MULTIPLE .h OR .c FILES.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Multi-File Project Structure:) Tj
T*
(   File 1: config.h \(Shared Header\)) Tj
T*
(   #ifndef CONFIG_H) Tj
T*
(   #define CONFIG_H) Tj
T*
(   extern int global_pcr_cycles; /* extern declaration */) Tj
T*
(   void initialize_pcr\(void\);) Tj
T*
(   #endif) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   File 2: config.c \(Physical Definition\)) Tj
T*
