/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain inline functions in C99, comparing them with preprocessor macros and detailing compiler inlining heuristics.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Inline Functions in C99: Inline vs Preprocessor Macros:) Tj
T*
(   1. Architectural Purpose of Inlining:) Tj
T*
(   Every function call incurs microprocessor overhead: pushing parameters, branching, creating) Tj
T*
(   stack frame, saving registers, and popping on return.) Tj
T*
(   For tiny functions \(1-3 lines\), call overhead often exceeds actual computational time!) Tj
T*
(   The 'inline' keyword suggests that the compiler eliminate call overhead by pasting the function) Tj
T*
(   body directly into the call site.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Comparison: inline Functions vs #define Macros:) Tj
T*
(   Feature inline Function #define Macro) Tj
T*
(   Evaluation Phase Compiler Semantic Phase Preprocessor Lexical Phase) Tj
T*
(   Type Safety Strict type checking No type safety \(text paste\)) Tj
T*
(   Side-Effect Bugs Safe: evaluates args once Dangerous: SQUARE\(x++\) bugs) Tj
T*
(   Debugging Symbolic debugger visible Invisible in debug stack) Tj
T*
(   Syntax Validation Full C grammar validation Raw textual substitution) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Macro Side-Effect Bug Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   #define SQUARE_MACRO\(x\) \(\(x\) * \(x\)\)) Tj
T*
(   inline int square_inline\(int x\) { return x * x; }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int val = 3;) Tj
T*
(   int r1 = SQUARE_MACRO\(val++\); /* Expands to \(\(val++\) * \(val++\)\) -> val incremented TWICE! */) Tj
T*
(   /* r1 = 3 * 4 = 12, val becomes 5! */) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   val = 3;) Tj
T*
(   int r2 = square_inline\(val++\); /* Evaluates val++ once \(3\), passes 3 -> returns 9! val is 4. */) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Compiler Heuristics:) Tj
T*
(   The inline keyword is a RECOMMENDATION, not a mandate. The compiler may decline inlining if:) Tj
T*
(   - Function contains recursion.) Tj
T*
(   - Function contains loops, switch statements, or large blocks.) Tj
T*
(   - Address of the function is taken via function pointer.) Tj
T*
ET

