/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail variadic functions in C using <stdarg.h>, implementing a custom formatting print function my_printf\(\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Variadic Functions and the <stdarg.h> Facility:) Tj
T*
(   1. Purpose:) Tj
T*
(   Variadic functions accept a variable number of arguments \(like printf or scanf\).) Tj
T*
(   Syntax requirement: Must have at least one mandatory named parameter before the ellipsis \(...\):) Tj
T*
(   void custom_logger\(int level, const char *format, ...\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Four <stdarg.h> Macros:) Tj
T*
(   - va_list: Pointer type representing the variable argument list context.) Tj
T*
(   - va_start\(va_list ap, last_named_arg\): Initializes ap to point to the first variadic argument.) Tj
T*
(   - va_arg\(va_list ap, type\): Retrieves the next argument as 'type' and advances ap.) Tj
T*
(   \(Note: Default argument promotion applies: char/short -> int; float -> double\).) Tj
T*
(   - va_end\(va_list ap\): Finalizes and cleans up ap before return.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Complete Custom Variadic Formatter Implementation:) Tj
T*
