T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Mutual Recursion and Forward Prototypes in C:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition:) Tj
T*
(   Mutual \(indirect\) recursion occurs when function A calls function B, and function B in turn) Tj
T*
(   calls function A.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Forward Prototype Mandate:) Tj
T*
(   C is a single-pass compiler that evaluates declarations linearly from top to bottom.) Tj
T*
(   If A calls B, B must be known before A. But B calls A, so A must be known before B!) Tj
T*
(   Resolution: Provide forward function prototypes at the top of the translation unit so the) Tj
T*
(   compiler recognizes both signatures before either definition is processed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Code Example \(Determining Parity of Non-Negative Integers\):) Tj
T*
