(   [Problem Statement]: Write an ANSI C program to search a sorted integer array using Recursive Binary Search, analyzing worst-case logarithmic complexity.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Recursive Binary Search Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   1. Divide-and-Conquer Principle:) Tj
T*
(   Given sorted array arr[low...high]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Compute midpoint: mid = low + \(high - low\) / 2 \(avoids integer overflow\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: If arr[mid] == target, element found.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: If target < arr[mid], search left half: binary_search\(arr, low, mid - 1, target\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: If target > arr[mid], search right half: binary_search\(arr, mid + 1, high, target\).) Tj
T*
(   Base case: low > high indicates target is not present.) Tj
T*
(   Time complexity: O\(log N\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Complete ANSI C Source Code:) Tj
T*
