(   [Problem Statement]: Write an ANSI C program to demonstrate a recursive power function x^n using binary exponentiation in O\(log n\) time.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Binary Exponentiation \(Fast Power Algorithm\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Formulation:) Tj
T*
(   Naive multiplication x * x * ... * x takes O\(n\) steps.) Tj
T*
(   Fast Binary Exponentiation:) Tj
T*
(   - If n == 0: x^0 = 1.) Tj
T*
(   - If n is even: x^n = \(x^\(n/2\)\)^2.) Tj
T*
(   - If n is odd: x^n = x * \(x^\(n - 1\)\).) Tj
T*
(   Halves the exponent in each step, executing in O\(log n\) time complexity.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Complete ANSI C Source Code:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   double power_fast_recursive\(double x, long long n\) {) Tj
T*
(   if \(n == 0\) return 1.0;) Tj
T*
(   if \(n < 0\) return 1.0 / power_fast_recursive\(x, -n\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   double half = power_fast_recursive\(x, n / 2\);) Tj
T*
(   if \(n % 2 == 0\) {) Tj
T*
(   return half * half;) Tj
T*
(   } else {) Tj
T*
(   return x * half * half;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int main\(void\) {) Tj
T*
(   double base = 2.0;) Tj
T*
(   long long exp = 10;) Tj
T*
(   printf\("%.2f^%lld = %.4f \(Expected: 1024.0\)\\n",) Tj
T*
(   base, exp, power_fast_recursive\(base, exp\)\);) Tj
T*
(   return 0;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
