(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the dangers of returning pointers or references to local stack-allocated variables from C functions.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Dangling Pointer Bug: Returning Addresses of Local Variables:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Problem:) Tj
T*
(   Local automatic variables allocated inside a function reside in that function's activation) Tj
T*
(   record on the stack.) Tj
T*
(   When the function returns, ITS STACK FRAME IS DEALLOCATED AND MARKED FOR REUSE.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Code Demonstrating the Fatal Bug:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
